  "solutions": [
    {
      "id": "sol.amc-10b-2019-p4.live",
      "kind": "proof-sketch",
      "text": "Let \\(d=b-a.\\)\n\nThen, we have \\[(a,b,c)= (a,a+d,a+2d).\\] Thus, \\[ax+(a+d)y=a+2d.\\] If we match the parts of \\(a\\) and \\(d,\\) we get \\[ax+ay=a\\] and \\[dy=2d\\] for all \\(a,d.\\) Therefore, we have \\[y=2,x+y=1\\] implying that \\[x=-1.\\] This makes the pair \\((-1,2).\\)\n\nThus, the answer is A .",
      "hints": [
        "Write \\(b=a+d\\) and \\(c=a+2d\\)",
        "The equation must hold for every possible \\(a\\) and \\(d\\)"
      ],
      "images": []
    }
  ],
